cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RadVeil: CPU-only face and ear anonymization for volumetric head imaging"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gródek"
    given-names: "Piotr"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rAum/radveil"
url: "https://rAum.github.io/radveil/"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-24
abstract: >-
  RadVeil removes identifiable facial and auricular (ear) surfaces from
  NIfTI head MRI and CT. It localizes the face the way an attacker would --
  rendering the volume as a portrait and running a 2D face detector -- and
  accepts an anonymization only when re-detection on the output fails. Ears
  are located from surface evidence (protrusion detection against a scalp
  baseline) rather than fixed anatomical offsets. Every voxel outside the
  exported mask is preserved bit-exact, with datatype, scaling and header
  intact.
keywords:
  - defacing
  - anonymization
  - de-identification
  - face removal
  - ear anonymization
  - biometric privacy
  - MRI
  - CT
  - NIfTI
  - DICOM
  - neuroimaging
  - medical imaging
